// Third capability type end-to-end: Args() reads process arguments, an ambient
// fingerprinting/exfiltration surface, now gated on PGY_CAP_ENV (op="args").
// Distinct bit + distinct require site from RANDOM/CLOCK. With the default grant
// it runs; under a host PGY_CAP_GRANT that omits "env" the runtime gate
// fail-closes (class=capability-denied), identically on C and LLVM. This closes
// the previously-dead PGY_CAP_ENV bit (the reader was ungated).
let a: Array<String> = Args();
Log("args ok");
